NOTE ON THE eBPF PROGRAMS (bpf/*.bpf.c): the eBPF/LSM programs are licensed
GPL, not MIT. The Linux kernel requires it -- an LSM BPF program must declare a
GPL-compatible license (`char LICENSE[] SEC("license") = "GPL";`) to call the
kernel helpers these programs use, so the GPL is forced by the kernel, not
chosen for style. The MIT license above covers the userspace code (agent,
daemon, dashboard, scripts, benchmarks, docs); the GPL covers the in-kernel BPF
programs. See README "License".
